{
  "_comment": "AEW (added Nov 15 2026). tracks: Dynamite (Wednesdays 8 PM ET, TBS/HBO Max), Collision (Saturdays 8 PM ET, TNT/HBO Max) and big events (pay-per-views); each has its own last-watched. accounts: official X handles without the @ (only AEW is confirmed). weak: everyday words and phrases (Dynamite, Collision, Full Gear, The Cut, The Elite, Swerve, PAC...); they only count with a context word, a second keyword, or on an air night. seasons: one per calendar year; that year's debuts, new names and factions go in its people and terms. Shows outside the US evening get \"airTime\" (US Eastern). Dates from AEW's events page, Fightful and Wrestling Inc. TO DO: Collision on Dec 19 (Worlds End day) and Dec 26 are taped but their air dates are unconfirmed, so they are left out; January 2027 weekly shows added Nov 16 (F4W: Collision live from Arlington Jan 9/16/23; Jan 30 Collision not announced; the Feb 3 Sugar Land taping's Collision air date unknown, probably Sat Feb 6); New Year's Smash (Fri Jan 1) and the UK shows (Dynasty, London Dynamite) use early airTimes until US start times are known; Revolution 2027 date. Then run npm test. Never delete or rename an episode id (users have ticked it); to remove one on purpose, also add its id to a \"removedEpisodes\" list, or the extension refuses the file. everyday: weak keywords so ordinary they need backup even on a show night (a wrestling word, a second name, or an author who has been posting about the show); distinctive names like Cody or Rhea stay out of it so they still count alone on show nights.",
